WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.590
- Okay, here we go.

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:04.320
Going in now to see the Vision Pro.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.700
No photos, no video?

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.533
- [Man] No.

00:00:06.533 --> 00:00:08.040
- So I have good news and bad news.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:08.873
The good news,

00:00:08.873 --> 00:00:12.330
I did get to try out Apple's
new Mixed Reality Headset.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.720
Bad news, Apple wouldn't
let us film me wearing it.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.640
Thus, we're here.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.640
They did let us film
the headset on a table.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:22.430
Roll that footage.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.050
(upbeat music)

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:28.710
But yes, I did get to spend 30
minutes wearing the headset,

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:31.200
which is really focused on
bringing digital objects

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:33.270
into your real world.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.920
Roll footage from the keynote.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.710
- [Presenter] Games on a
giant screen surrounded

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.810
by spatial audio,

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:44.220
and connect with people as if
you're sharing the same space.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.350
- I got to see a few of
those demos in the headset,

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:50.370
which is by far the best
AR/VR headset I've ever used,

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:52.710
but it's still a headset.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.650
Let me take you through it from here.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.230
Let's start with what it's
like to wear this thing.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:01.600
Honestly, it felt like Apple
stuck a giant Apple Watch

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.680
to my head, in a good way.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.840
The sock-like headband was easy to put on

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.240
and adjust the size with the knob.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.020
Oh, look, Tim Cook showed
up, not wearing the headset.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.640
For the first 15 minutes of the demo,

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.950
I couldn't believe how comfortable it was,

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.043
far cozier than the Meta
Quests Pro or the Quest 2.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.980
A lot of that is because
the battery lives in a pack

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.750
that's attached to the headset.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.312
Behold, battery pack footage.

00:01:27.312 --> 00:01:30.300
(upbeat music)

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.450
Honestly, the battery, which
is said to last only two hours,

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:36.450
was pretty light and easy
to fit in my back pocket,

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.030
but it's still a lot of tech on your face.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.050
By the end of the demo,

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:43.590
the top of my nose and forehead
started to feel the weight.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.933
Here's a photo of me when I took it off.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.100
I guess this is why so much
of the footage from Apple

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.130
is of people alone in their homes.

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:54.150
- [Presenter] With a spatial cinema

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:57.570
that transforms any space,
like this apartment,

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:59.880
you have a gorgeous screen you can adjust

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.470
to the perfect size.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:02.790
- Apple says that discomfort

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.820
was because it only had
limited sized light seals,

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.190
which fit the headset to your face.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:09.420
There will be more options

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.360
when the device is
available early next year.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.820
Okay, so what's it like to
look through this thing?

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:15.780
Pretty insane,

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:18.150
especially compared to
other headsets out there.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:21.300
Apple is really focusing on
blending the digital world

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.590
with your real world,

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:25.770
and you can really toggle
between a VR-like experience

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.540
where you're in a virtual world,

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.480
and an AR-like experience
where digital objects show up

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.100
in your real world.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.960
Spin the digital crown one way

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.640
and you'll see more of the real world,

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.130
spin it the other and you see less.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:41.130
Press on the button and you
get taken to the home screen,

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.920
and it, again, really worked like that.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:44.753
Even better,

00:02:44.753 --> 00:02:47.040
looking at the real world
looks crisp and clear,

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.340
unlike the Meta Quests Pro
where things can look grainy.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:52.770
But going back and forth between AR and VR

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:54.510
did make me feel a little bit queasy

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:55.800
by the end of the demo.

00:02:55.800 --> 00:03:00.090
It wasn't like a puke situation,
but you know, just, nah.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.640
Unlike other VR headsets,
there are no controllers,

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.890
so your eyes are your cursor

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:08.010
and your fingers are
like the mouse buttons.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:11.130
To select things, you
just pinch like this.

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.270
And then to scroll,

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.583
you move it in different directions.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.960
And yes, one of the craziest
things is the front screen,

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:22.170
where people who look at
you can see your eyes.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.090
No, I didn't test this,

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:25.990
but look at what we made in Photoshop.

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:28.803
Okay, so what do you do with it?

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.700
During the demo, I was able to
scatter a few apps in space,

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.530
so instead of having multiple monitors,

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.600
you could just look at
these virtual screens

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.190
around your room.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:40.020
I was also able to have a FaceTime chat

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.960
with an Apple employee, except
it wasn't a video of her,

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:45.720
it was a 3D hologram of her.

00:03:45.720 --> 00:03:47.970
During the call, she was
able to launch a presentation

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.070
for us to work together on.

00:03:50.070 --> 00:03:51.240
And the coolest thing was probably

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.970
the 3D spatial photos and videos.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.370
A dedicated button on the
top left of the headset

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:59.010
will allow wearers to snap these photos,

00:03:59.010 --> 00:04:01.080
though I couldn't try it myself.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.413
And I watched a 3D movie
clip and was very into it.

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.550
Do we need more things to
do with the Vision Pro,

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:12.630
especially to justify
its $3,500 price tag?

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:13.710
Absolutely,

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:16.110
but that's why Apple's getting
it out now to developers

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.900
so they can dream up new experiences.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:21.540
Are we all gonna buy this
when it comes out next year?

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:22.373
Nope.

00:04:22.373 --> 00:04:25.920
But this vision of spatial
computing, as Apple calls it,

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:28.380
and seeing the digital in our real world

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:31.710
really does feel like the next big thing,

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:34.230
even if it does seem,
at its present moment,

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:37.140
a bit dystopian and isolating.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:39.690
And I do look forward to
trying the Vision Pro again

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:42.450
and filming what's actually happening,

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:44.925
instead of more of this.

00:04:44.925 --> 00:04:47.592
(upbeat music)

